WEBVTT

00:17.510 --> 00:19.660
Well, well.

00:19.980 --> 00:22.410
Now this is splendid.

00:22.410 --> 00:26.920
These are the earnings 
from this Workshop Battle.

00:26.920 --> 00:30.050
This much already?

00:30.340 --> 00:32.880
Now that's funky.

00:33.190 --> 00:35.890
It's merely the 30th floor,

00:38.180 --> 00:40.700
but there's the new Slayer Candidate...

00:48.660 --> 00:51.450
the popular Princess of Jahad...

00:52.680 --> 00:56.680
and Yama's Mad Dog, said to be 
the strongest E-rank Regular.

00:58.130 --> 01:01.810
On top of that, they have the 
White Heavenly Mirror and

01:01.810 --> 01:04.660
Blood Tamara made by Io and Funk.

01:04.950 --> 01:09.720
Furthermore, spectators aboard the ship can

01:09.720 --> 01:14.940
bet on games and directly 
influence the results.

01:14.940 --> 01:19.070
If anything, it's impossible 
not to make money.

01:19.550 --> 01:24.680
We'll make hundreds of times more than 
this during tomorrow's tournament.

01:25.200 --> 01:28.940
Are we sure this is okay? 
What if the teachers find out?

01:29.220 --> 01:31.320
There's no need for concern.

01:31.320 --> 01:33.610
Even if they hear about it,

01:33.610 --> 01:37.320
as long as your research is 
completed, no one will complain.

01:37.320 --> 01:41.560
You need only trust me.

01:42.010 --> 01:46.830
I promise to make this Workshop 
Battle the ultimate show,

01:47.100 --> 01:50.080
for the sake of your research, as well.

01:51.590 --> 01:53.840
We'll speak again later.

02:00.080 --> 02:02.850
Can we really trust him?

02:03.350 --> 02:07.080
He's undoubtedly a skilled businessman,

02:07.080 --> 02:09.850
but there are rumors he's associated 
with some sketchy individuals.

02:09.850 --> 02:12.730
What are you so worried about?

02:12.730 --> 02:16.990
All we need to do is conduct our 
research using the money he makes.

02:16.990 --> 02:21.490
After all, once Emily is complete,
 it will all be over.

02:28.010 --> 02:30.310
Now that's funky.

04:00.970 --> 04:04.970
<b>Episode 17</b>

04:00.970 --> 04:04.970
<b>Funky!</b>

04:09.720 --> 04:11.140
Where should we go next?

04:11.140 --> 04:12.080
Huh?

04:18.700 --> 04:21.190
You think you can sit here drooling over girls?!

04:21.190 --> 04:24.110
You nearly destroyed our team!

04:24.110 --> 04:26.700
Ow, ow! You're gonna break my back!

04:27.880 --> 04:30.060
I see you two still get along great.

04:30.060 --> 04:32.960
You call this getting along, Mei?!

04:33.410 --> 04:35.580
Good to see you again, Shibisu.

04:35.580 --> 04:41.060
If you're here, that means the strongest 
E-rank Regular is here, too.

04:41.060 --> 04:42.600
I'm not so happy about that.

04:43.980 --> 04:46.730
But I'm glad you all seem to be doing well.

04:47.560 --> 04:50.010
I don't know that we are.

04:50.670 --> 04:54.480
Hatz's sword was broken, and Amigo...

04:54.740 --> 04:58.430
Anyway, I heard the princess 
got up to something again.

04:58.430 --> 05:02.480
They say she received a special boarding 
pass for catching a stowaway.

05:02.840 --> 05:04.120
Apparently.

05:04.460 --> 05:06.740
I don't know the details, either.

05:07.190 --> 05:12.590
<i>We heard you received a bonus ticket for 
catching a stowaway on the Archimedes.</i>

05:12.590 --> 05:18.750
<i>Catching him went great, but there 
were no tickets left by then.</i>

05:18.750 --> 05:22.420
But then a Bongbong showed up, and...

05:23.310 --> 05:24.510
And then?

05:24.510 --> 05:28.760
I'm not sure exactly what happened, but 
I was transported here when I shot it.

05:28.760 --> 05:30.890
Management said it was a thank-you gift.

05:30.890 --> 05:34.670
Splendid as always, Princess Endorsi.

05:34.670 --> 05:39.050
Well, I'm tired. That's 
enough interview questions.

05:39.050 --> 05:42.020
Wait! If we could just speak 
with you a little longer...

05:47.080 --> 05:48.990
Jue Viole Grace!

05:48.990 --> 05:50.660
It's the Slayer Candidate!

05:51.690 --> 05:56.650
Spectators are hoping for a 
showdown between you and Viole.

05:56.650 --> 06:00.480
If you face each other in the tournament, 
how do you think it will turn out?

06:00.480 --> 06:03.670
Didn't I say this interview is over?

06:07.740 --> 06:12.410
That isn't Jue Viole Grace.
He's the 25th Bam.

06:16.420 --> 06:18.310
Hey, wait!

06:18.650 --> 06:21.310
You're going to sell me for a ticket?

06:21.550 --> 06:24.040
And you call yourself a Princess of Jahad?!

06:28.210 --> 06:29.500
Please!

06:33.450 --> 06:35.040
Please help me.

06:35.260 --> 06:38.260
Without me, Emily will die!

06:38.830 --> 06:40.730
Stop! Let go!

06:41.980 --> 06:44.130
Emily can't die.

06:44.130 --> 06:46.560
She's an app. What are you talking about?

06:46.560 --> 06:48.980
Emily isn't an app.

06:48.980 --> 06:51.550
She's on board this ship.

06:51.550 --> 06:53.180
That's enough out of you!

06:53.420 --> 06:58.320
I used to be a lonely bastard,
but Emily gave me a reason to live!

06:58.320 --> 06:59.810
I owe her my life!

07:00.200 --> 07:04.530
Man, why have there been so 
many stowaways recently?

07:15.740 --> 07:16.990
Emily...

07:26.720 --> 07:29.470
Hey, so... I know I've 
asked a bunch of times,

07:29.700 --> 07:33.510
but you're sure this gator 
doesn't bite, right?

07:33.510 --> 07:36.600
Who are you calling a gator, Curry Turtle?

07:36.600 --> 07:38.460
What? Curry Turtle?

07:38.850 --> 07:40.060
Are you talking about me?

07:40.060 --> 07:44.350
He's a stupid gator who can't 
remember people's names.

07:44.350 --> 07:45.880
Shut up, turtles!

07:45.880 --> 07:47.730
I'm not an alligator!

07:47.730 --> 07:50.480
I'm the great Rak Wraithraiser!

07:52.950 --> 07:56.920
Forget it. I'll handle this.

07:56.920 --> 07:57.990
All right.

07:57.990 --> 08:00.750
Then you can look after the gator.

08:00.750 --> 08:03.000
Who are you calling a gator?!

08:03.000 --> 08:05.900
I'll eat the damn bastard.

08:05.900 --> 08:09.060
How much do you know?

08:09.470 --> 08:15.010
From "the Yellow Turtle betrayed us" 
to "the Black Turtle is still alive."

08:15.640 --> 08:18.320
I heard everything you know.

08:19.040 --> 08:20.020
From who?

08:20.510 --> 08:22.000
The Red Turtle.

08:22.000 --> 08:23.640
Hwaryun, huh?

08:24.260 --> 08:28.820
<i>She told me not to say anything, so why...</i>

08:29.990 --> 08:31.650
Blue Turtle.

08:32.150 --> 08:34.620
What are you hesitating for?

08:36.750 --> 08:37.670
What?

08:37.670 --> 08:39.410
Khun's friend?

08:39.410 --> 08:43.160
Yeah. It sounded like they were old friends.

08:43.160 --> 08:45.920
His friend, huh?

08:47.920 --> 08:51.160
This gelatin is so jiggly and awesome!

08:51.160 --> 08:53.760
What are you even doing here?!

08:53.760 --> 08:55.560
It's not like we can help it.

08:55.560 --> 08:58.560
We were assigned to the same room.

08:58.560 --> 09:01.930
Don't worry. We won't do anything.

09:01.930 --> 09:03.430
Actually...

09:04.240 --> 09:05.830
Aren't you guys missing some members?

09:12.060 --> 09:14.190
Damn that gator.

09:17.020 --> 09:18.200
An alligator?

09:18.420 --> 09:24.960
Did you sneak out last night so you could 
show me that pathetic look on your face?

09:25.270 --> 09:28.140
We're gonna go bring back the 
Black Turtle this instant!

09:28.140 --> 09:32.710
You idiot! Do you think FUG would 
just let a Slayer Candidate go?

09:32.710 --> 09:36.300
And if Jahad learns Bam is alive—

09:39.710 --> 09:44.220
You're just a turtle! Stop worrying 
about complicated things!

09:44.700 --> 09:45.590
He hit him!

09:45.590 --> 09:47.320
Awesome!

09:47.320 --> 09:50.110
Forget it! I'll bring him back.

09:50.700 --> 09:53.890
I'm telling you,
there's nothing we can do right now!

09:54.360 --> 09:56.870
You mean there's nothing <i>you</i> can do.

09:57.820 --> 09:59.880
What are you trying to accomplish?

09:59.880 --> 10:04.620
If you keep being indecisive, 
you'll ruin everything.

10:05.050 --> 10:07.600
You haven't changed a bit.

10:10.630 --> 10:12.000
Don't make me laugh.

10:12.000 --> 10:14.130
What?! Laugh?!

10:14.340 --> 10:17.260
Are you mocking me just because I shrank?!

10:17.260 --> 10:19.870
Hey, look at me! Wimpy Turtle!

10:19.870 --> 10:21.260
Hey, Wimpy Turtle!

10:19.870 --> 10:21.260
Hey, calm down!

10:35.000 --> 10:36.780
Goseng made this.

10:37.750 --> 10:39.880
Miseng and Prince liked it.

10:43.590 --> 10:46.120
You must be really good friends

10:46.820 --> 10:49.930
for you to blow your lid arguing about him.

10:49.930 --> 10:51.540
Good friends?

10:52.320 --> 10:54.800
We just spent some time 
together on the 2nd floor.

10:54.800 --> 10:58.340
You never speak your true feelings, do you?

10:58.340 --> 10:59.270
Huh?

10:59.270 --> 11:03.180
If I had a close friend,
I'd try to do everything together.

11:03.540 --> 11:05.030
But you're different.

11:05.400 --> 11:07.310
You shoulder everything alone,

11:08.030 --> 11:10.300
even though it overwhelms you.

11:10.720 --> 11:12.810
You're an awkward guy.

11:16.470 --> 11:18.450
What? Are you mad?

11:19.420 --> 11:20.820
Maybe it's a habit

11:21.660 --> 11:23.320
from my childhood.

11:31.800 --> 11:35.160
Acquiring a precious 
gemstone makes me anxious.

11:36.050 --> 11:38.460
Instead of displaying it, I hide it away.

11:42.770 --> 11:47.720
Not once do I wear it on my finger.

11:48.810 --> 11:50.030
I see.

11:51.150 --> 11:54.730
Then this time, instead of hiding it,
let's share it with the others.

11:55.080 --> 11:55.960
Hey.

12:07.310 --> 12:08.300
You want some?

12:09.340 --> 12:15.760
What? If you're hoping for something as 
sickening as reconciliation, give me a break.

12:17.580 --> 12:19.070
It made me happy.

12:19.070 --> 12:19.760
Huh?

12:20.300 --> 12:22.780
When I learned the Black Turtle
was still alive.

12:23.360 --> 12:25.960
When I heard I'd get to see you again here.

12:26.690 --> 12:29.260
I thought the three of us would get 
to climb the Tower together again.

12:30.420 --> 12:32.770
But you're different.

12:33.430 --> 12:37.290
You're a cowardly and evil-natured 
turtle who worries about everything.

12:37.700 --> 12:39.780
Did you come to pick a fight?

12:40.270 --> 12:45.780
I just wanted to share my joy 
with you and the Black Turtle.

12:46.520 --> 12:49.280
Don't celebrate yet.

12:50.920 --> 12:54.790
At tomorrow's Workshop Battle,
I'll pummel the FUG

12:55.670 --> 12:58.870
until the grand prize and Bam are mine.

13:00.370 --> 13:03.550
Was it all right to let the dinosaur go?

13:03.550 --> 13:06.520
I hope they don't get into another fight.

13:06.520 --> 13:08.270
I'm sure they'll be fine.

13:08.270 --> 13:09.430
What makes you say that?

13:09.690 --> 13:13.180
Khun once told me about his friends.

13:13.820 --> 13:18.160
Khun's mom was strict with 
him ever since he was a kid.

13:17.180 --> 13:18.750
This is so good, too!

13:18.750 --> 13:22.690
He went through a lot of 
hard times after that, too.

13:19.010 --> 13:21.070
Chocolate is awesome!

13:21.650 --> 13:22.690
I'm so glad to be human!

13:23.380 --> 13:26.700
That's when he met Rak and the others.

13:27.220 --> 13:31.420
For Khun, it must've been an 
unforgettably fun experience.

13:35.700 --> 13:38.710
Blue Turtle, have you finally bounced back?

13:38.710 --> 13:40.280
Don't be absurd.

13:40.280 --> 13:42.960
I was never hesitating.

13:47.030 --> 13:48.890
Look forward to it.

13:49.310 --> 13:53.690
I swear I'll take back Bam 
at tomorrow's tournament

13:53.690 --> 13:57.410
using methods far more 
underhanded than FUG's.

14:15.290 --> 14:17.140
You're certain that's true?

14:17.140 --> 14:19.250
Sounds like you still don't believe me.

14:24.650 --> 14:26.260
<i>What are they doing here?</i>

14:39.410 --> 14:41.470
We're here, Ilmar.

14:41.470 --> 14:42.280
Huh?

14:54.730 --> 14:56.170
Ilmar?

14:57.940 --> 15:01.170
Boys shouldn't be so quick to cry.

15:01.870 --> 15:04.670
You need to become strong 
enough to protect others.

15:07.300 --> 15:08.990
I know you can do it.

15:13.460 --> 15:15.050
Dr. Sophia!

15:16.490 --> 15:17.680
My, my.

15:18.340 --> 15:20.060
You've grown into a fine man.

15:21.060 --> 15:24.290
But I see you're still a crybaby.

15:24.940 --> 15:26.320
Doctor...

15:27.210 --> 15:29.570
It's good to see you again, Ilmar.

15:30.330 --> 15:33.090
Why are you spying on them?

15:35.870 --> 15:37.280
Is it that interesting?

15:40.550 --> 15:43.830
What's this? Are you going to play with me?

15:44.460 --> 15:45.570
Who's there?

15:46.920 --> 15:48.340
You...

15:53.820 --> 15:59.390
I don't know how you got in here, but stay 
there until the Workshop Battle ends.

15:59.390 --> 16:00.100
Bastard!

16:00.360 --> 16:01.650
What do you think you're doing?!

16:01.980 --> 16:04.540
Doctor, who is that boy?

16:04.540 --> 16:06.610
Let me introduce you.

16:06.610 --> 16:08.080
This boy's name is—

16:08.080 --> 16:11.240
I'm not interested in defective products.

16:11.240 --> 16:13.310
Come on, Beta!

16:14.400 --> 16:17.240
I'm sorry. He's intensely shy.

16:17.740 --> 16:20.810
He's your younger brother.

16:20.810 --> 16:22.120
Younger brother?

16:22.690 --> 16:23.870
Follow me.

16:23.870 --> 16:27.310
I'll show you the research I've been doing.

16:43.230 --> 16:44.800
Look.

16:46.480 --> 16:50.410
This is Emily, the subject of my research.

16:52.520 --> 16:55.520
This is Emily?

16:52.760 --> 16:56.600
I love you... I love you...

16:58.100 --> 17:03.120
When she wakes up, she'll be an incredible 
weapon that will shake the entire Tower.

17:04.530 --> 17:05.930
Good afternoon.

17:06.400 --> 17:07.290
Good afternoon.

17:14.730 --> 17:17.800
The long wait is over, everyone.

17:17.800 --> 17:22.320
The E-rank Regular Workshop 
Battle will begin shortly.

17:33.080 --> 17:34.570
Jue Viole Grace!

17:35.070 --> 17:37.210
I've been wanting to meet you.

17:37.820 --> 17:40.950
My family was destroyed by the Ten Families.

17:41.310 --> 17:45.330
We believe you'll avenge us.

17:45.660 --> 17:48.420
Crush those bastards for us, okay?

17:54.830 --> 17:57.220
What's that face for?

17:57.920 --> 17:59.120
Xia Xia.

17:59.610 --> 18:01.970
Are you thinking about what 
that kid said to you earlier?

18:02.720 --> 18:07.920
Do you hold a grudge against 
Jahad and the Ten Families, too?

18:08.230 --> 18:09.710
Is that why you...

18:09.710 --> 18:10.980
Yeah, right.

18:10.980 --> 18:14.900
I'm doing this because you can benefit me.

18:14.900 --> 18:16.990
As long as I'm making money,
I'm fine with it.

18:18.040 --> 18:19.090
I'm glad to hear that.

18:19.400 --> 18:22.990
Why? Because you can hate me 
without reservations now?

18:23.600 --> 18:27.330
I'm glad nothing bad happened to you.

18:32.300 --> 18:33.420
What's his deal?

18:35.020 --> 18:37.520
Were you tormenting him again?

18:37.520 --> 18:38.510
Huh?

18:38.510 --> 18:41.260
Also, could you not act like we're friends?

18:41.970 --> 18:43.590
We're enemies, aren't we?

18:45.430 --> 18:50.770
I don't know what you want from him, 
but I don't think it'll go the way you expect.

18:52.260 --> 18:53.940
This place is full of people

18:53.940 --> 18:57.540
who think only of using others as 
stepping stones to get ahead,

18:58.070 --> 18:59.280
but he's different.

18:59.950 --> 19:03.030
It's like he gives off light.

19:04.400 --> 19:06.520
I'd leave him alone if I were you.

19:08.470 --> 19:14.120
There are those who will follow him 
anywhere after seeing that light.

19:15.830 --> 19:18.800
Is Hatz really not going to participate?

19:18.800 --> 19:21.210
He hasn't been back since yesterday.

19:21.620 --> 19:22.930
Forget him.

19:23.280 --> 19:27.810
Aw, man. If only Khun were here.

19:31.190 --> 19:35.360
The E-rank Regular Workshop 
Battle will now begin.

19:35.730 --> 19:37.650
We'll be your hosts, Io...

19:37.650 --> 19:40.450
...and Funk.

19:40.850 --> 19:47.090
We'd like to express our gratitude 
to the guests gathered here.

19:48.950 --> 19:52.960
The first game in the Workshop 
Battle is called Flag.

19:53.350 --> 19:58.980
The first three out of eight Regulars 
to put their flag in one of these holes

19:58.980 --> 20:00.740
will advance.

20:01.170 --> 20:03.410
Letting go of your flag

20:03.410 --> 20:07.900
or dropping it outside the arena 
will result in disqualification.

20:07.900 --> 20:11.010
Even if fewer than three Regulars remain,

20:11.010 --> 20:14.100
the game will continue until 
their flags have been inserted.

20:14.340 --> 20:20.010
This game is an individual battle, 
but simply winning isn't enough.

20:20.390 --> 20:25.370
The team leaders will bet 
on this game as Gamblers.

20:25.620 --> 20:29.780
The top six leaders who finish 
with the most points will

20:29.780 --> 20:32.640
get to participate in the final tournament.

20:32.640 --> 20:36.420
In other words, it's both an 
individual and a team game.

20:36.420 --> 20:38.920
<b>Group 1 Participants

 Johnson
 Leg
 Bulgasario
 Rek Curtain
 Ja Wangnan
 Hon Akraptor
 Yeon Miseng
 Prince</b>

20:36.910 --> 20:38.920
The group 1 participants are

20:39.290 --> 20:44.810
Johnson, Leg, Bulgasario, 
Rek Curtain, Ja Wangnan,

20:44.810 --> 20:48.430
Hon Akraptor, Yeon Miseng, and Prince.

20:48.930 --> 20:50.680
Miseng and Prince?

20:51.050 --> 20:53.940
So they're okay!

20:55.180 --> 20:56.940
I'm so glad.

20:57.850 --> 20:59.900
<i>The game will begin shortly.</i>

20:59.900 --> 21:04.400
<i>Gamblers, please predict the 
winners of the first group.</i>

21:04.400 --> 21:05.200
<i>Now...</i>

21:05.740 --> 21:07.200
Place your bets!

21:09.230 --> 21:11.200
The betting has ended.

21:11.200 --> 21:13.700
Then let us begin!

21:13.700 --> 21:16.500
Open the doors!

21:24.440 --> 21:26.300
Prince! Miseng!

21:26.300 --> 21:27.720
We're here to save you!

21:29.720 --> 21:33.360
P-Prince? What happened to your face?

21:34.160 --> 21:36.370
Ak, Wangnan! Run!

21:36.370 --> 21:37.350
Huh?

21:40.360 --> 21:43.110
You have to run! She's coming!

21:43.640 --> 21:45.110
What are you talking about?

21:54.970 --> 21:56.650
M-Miseng?

21:58.030 --> 21:59.000
Run!

22:00.650 --> 22:05.010
She's lost her mind!

23:37.990 --> 23:39.430
So good!

23:39.040 --> 23:41.250
<b>Next Time
The Mad Dog and the Lizard</b>

23:39.430 --> 23:40.980
What a horrible combination!
